IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc8-nouns`
IMPORT `roc8-order-34`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), Order 34: TESTS.  Every expected value is written from the text of the
-- paragraph named beside it, before running.  The "last day" and the "first day" are made-up dates standing in for
-- O 3 r 3's count (S-T1, S-T1b); the lead's merge replaces them with calls.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `test fixtures`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`o 34 r 2 test kind s 15(4)` MEANS `o 34 r 2(1)(a) application to challenge an arbitrator under section 15(4)`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 16` MEANS `o 34 r 2(1)(b) application to remove an arbitrator under section 16`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 21(9)` MEANS `o 34 r 2(1)(c) application to decide on the arbitral tribunal's ruling on jurisdiction under section 21(9)`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` MEANS `o 34 r 2(1)(d) application to determine a question of law under section 45`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` MEANS `o 34 r 2(1)(e) application to set aside an award under section 48`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(b)` MEANS `o 34 r 2(1)(f) application for permission to appeal under section 49(3)(b)`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(a)` MEANS `o 34 r 2(2) appeal on a question of law under section 49(3)(a)`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 6(4)` MEANS `o 34 r 3(1)(a) application to reinstate discontinued proceedings under section 6(4)`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 28(4)` MEANS `o 34 r 3(1)(b) application for permission to enforce interim orders or directions of an arbitral tribunal under section 28(4)`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` MEANS `o 34 r 3(1)(c) application for an order in support of arbitral proceedings under section 31`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 10 or 36` MEANS `o 34 r 3(1)(d) application for an extension of time under section 10 or 36`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 41(2)` MEANS `o 34 r 3(1)(e) application for an order under section 41(2) where the arbitral tribunal withholds its award for non-payment of fees and expenses`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` MEANS `o 34 r 3(1)(f) application for permission to enforce an award under section 37 or 46`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 56` MEANS `o 34 r 3(1)(g) application to hear an application in open court under section 56`
`o 34 r 2 test kind s 57` MEANS `o 34 r 3(1)(h) application for directions on publishing information relating to an application heard in private under section 57`
`o 34 r 2 test kind other` MEANS `o 34 r 2 other application`

`o 34 test d1` MEANS Date 1 3 2026
`o 34 test d10` MEANS Date 10 3 2026
`o 34 test d15` MEANS Date 15 3 2026
`o 34 test d16` MEANS Date 16 3 2026
`o 34 test d20` MEANS Date 20 3 2026

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 34 r 5(2) supporting affidavit`
`o 34 r 5(2) test affidavit` MEANS `o 34 r 5(2) supporting affidavit` WITH
    `o 34 r 5(2)(a) it has exhibited to it a copy of the arbitration agreement or any record of the content of the arbitration agreement` IS a
    `o 34 r 5(2)(a) it has exhibited to it the award` IS b
    `o 34 r 5(2)(a) it has exhibited to it every other document relied on by the applicant` IS c
    `o 34 r 5(2)(b) it sets out any evidence relied on by the claimant` IS d
    `o 34 r 5(2)(c) it is served with the originating application` IS e

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 34 r 6(1) originating application for the appeal`
`o 34 r 6(1) test application` MEANS `o 34 r 6(1) originating application for the appeal` WITH
    `o 34 r 6(1)(a) it states that the appeal is being brought with the agreement of all the other parties` IS a
    `o 34 r 6(1)(b) it identifies the award` IS b
    `o 34 r 6(1)(c) it states as briefly as possible the questions of law which will be raised in the appeal` IS c

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 34 r 6(4) appellant's Case`
`o 34 r 6(4) test Case` MEANS `o 34 r 6(4) appellant's Case` WITH
    `o 34 r 6(4)(a) it contains a statement in numbered paragraphs of each ground on which it is sought to contend that the tribunal erred in law` IS a
    `o 34 r 6(4)(b) it makes references to the paragraph or passage of the award where each alleged error is to be found` IS b

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 34 r 6(8) core bundle of documents`
`o 34 r 6(8) test bundle` MEANS `o 34 r 6(8) core bundle of documents` WITH
    `o 34 r 6(8)(a) it contains a copy of the award` IS a
    `o 34 r 6(8)(b) it contains other documents that are relevant to any question in the appeal or which are referred to in the appellant's Case` IS b
    `o 34 r 6(8)(c) it contains an index of the documents included in the core bundle` IS c

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 34 r 7(1) originating application for permission`
`o 34 r 7(1) test application` MEANS `o 34 r 7(1) originating application for permission` WITH
    `o 34 r 7(1) it is for an order that such permission be granted` IS a
    `o 34 r 7(1) it is for a further order that, in the event that permission is granted, the appeal be heard and determined` IS b
    `o 34 r 7(2) it identifies the award` IS c
    `o 34 r 7(2) it states as briefly as possible the questions of law which will be raised in the appeal` IS d

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 34 r 7(4) affidavit in support of the application for permission`
`o 34 r 7(4) test affidavit` MEANS `o 34 r 7(4) affidavit in support of the application for permission` WITH
    `o 34 r 7(4) it exhibits a copy of the award` IS a
    `o 34 r 7(4) it sets out any evidence relied on by the claimant for the purpose of satisfying the Court of the matters mentioned in section 49(5)` IS b
    `o 34 r 7(4) it sets out any evidence relied on by the claimant for the purpose of satisfying the Court that permission should be granted` IS c

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 34 r 13 affidavit supporting the application for permission to enforce`
`o 34 r 13 test affidavit` MEANS `o 34 r 13 affidavit supporting the application for permission to enforce` WITH
    `o 34 r 13(a) it exhibits a copy of the arbitration agreement or any record of the content of the arbitration agreement` IS a
    `o 34 r 13(a) it exhibits the original order or direction made by the arbitral tribunal sought to be enforced` IS b
    `o 34 r 13(b) it states the provisions of the Act or the applicable rules adopted in the arbitration on which the applicant relies` IS c

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 34 r 14(1) affidavit supporting the application for permission to enforce an award`
`o 34 r 14(1) test affidavit` MEANS `o 34 r 14(1) affidavit supporting the application for permission to enforce an award` WITH
    `o 34 r 14(1)(a) it exhibits the arbitration agreement or any record of the content of the arbitration agreement (the original or a copy)` IS a
    `o 34 r 14(1)(a) it exhibits the original award or a copy of it` IS b
    `o 34 r 14(1)(b) it states the name and the usual or last known place of residence or business of the creditor` IS c
    `o 34 r 14(1)(b) it states the name and the usual or last known place of residence or business of the debtor` IS d
    `o 34 r 14(1)(c) it states either that the award has not been complied with or the extent to which it has not been complied with at the date of the application` IS e

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- "Act" means the Arbitration Act.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 the Act is the Arbitration Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 the Act is the Arbitration Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a reference to a section is, unless otherwise expressly provided, a reference to a section in the Act.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "appellate court" and "arbitral tribunal" have the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act (not among the sources).
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 appellate court has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 appellate court has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 appellate court has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 arbitral tribunal has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 arbitral tribunal has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 1 arbitral tribunal has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- matters for a Judge in person`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- r 2(1): every application to a Judge under (a) to (f) must be made by originating application.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 15(4)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 16` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 21(9)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(b)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not made to a Judge: the paragraph is limited to applications to a Judge.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an application the paragraph does not name.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(a)` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 2(2): an appeal with the agreement of all the other parties under s 49(3)(a).
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(2) the appeal must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(a)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(2) the appeal must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(a)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(2) the appeal must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the way the application is made (the compliance twins of rules 2(1), 2(2) and 3(2)); a summons gets NOTHING (judgment call QB)
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons without notice` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating claim` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE `o 34 r 2 in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 15(4)` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(b)` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(2) the appeal is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(a)` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(2) the appeal is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(a)` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(2) the appeal is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(a)` FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(2) the appeal is made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- matters for a Judge or the Registrar`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 6(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 28(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 10 or 36` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 41(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 56` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 57` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 15(4)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` EQUALS NOTHING
-- compliance: made to a Judge, or to the Registrar, but not to a District Judge.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application is made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` `A Judge` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application is made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` `The Registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application is made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` `A District Judge` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the application is made to a Judge or the Registrar` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` `A Judge` EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 3(2): where an action is pending, summons in the action; in any other case, originating application.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application must be made by summons in the action` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application must be made by summons in the action` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application must be made by summons in the action` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application must be made by originating application` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the way the application is made under paragraph (2): summons where an action is pending, originating application otherwise
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons without notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 31` FALSE `o 34 r 2 by summons in the action` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(2) the application is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application` EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 3(3): without notice where urgent, or an application under s 37 or 46.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) this paragraph permits the application to be made without notice` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 6(4)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) this paragraph permits the application to be made without notice` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) this paragraph permits the application to be made without notice` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 6(4)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) this paragraph permits the application to be made without notice` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the way: summons without notice where an action is pending, originating application without notice otherwise.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) the application without notice is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` FALSE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by summons without notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) the application without notice is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` FALSE TRUE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) the application without notice is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` FALSE FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) the application without notice is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` FALSE FALSE `o 34 r 2 by summons without notice` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) the application without notice is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 6(4)` FALSE FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(3) the application without notice is made in the way this paragraph names` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` TRUE FALSE `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The two helpers that decide whether the application is one that paragraph (1) of rule 2 or of rule 3 names.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (f)` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 15(4)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (f)` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(b)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (f)` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 49(3)(a)` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (f)` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 37 or 46` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 2(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (f)` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (h)` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 6(4)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (h)` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 57` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (h)` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 3(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (h)` `o 34 r 2 test kind other` EQUALS FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- preliminary question of law`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT (`o 34 r 4(1) the period for making and serving the application`'s `period length`) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT (`o 34 r 4(1) the period for making and serving the application`'s `period unit`) EQUALS Days
#ASSERT (`o 34 r 4(1) the period for making and serving the application`'s `period direction`) EQUALS `After the anchor`
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the application must be made by originating application and served` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the application must be made by originating application and served` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the date after which the period runs` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` `o 34 r 4(1)(a) the agreement of all the parties to the arbitral proceedings` `o 34 test d1` `o 34 test d10` EQUALS JUST `o 34 test d1`
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the date after which the period runs` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` `o 34 r 4(1)(b) the permission of the arbitral tribunal` `o 34 test d1` `o 34 test d10` EQUALS JUST `o 34 test d10`
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the date after which the period runs` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` `o 34 r 4(1)(a) the agreement of all the parties to the arbitral proceedings` `o 34 test d1` `o 34 test d10` EQUALS NOTHING
-- in time: made and served on or before the last day (here the 15th).
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the application is made and served in time` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` `o 34 test d15` `o 34 test d15` `o 34 test d15` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the application is made and served in time` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` `o 34 test d16` `o 34 test d15` `o 34 test d15` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the application is made and served in time` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` `o 34 test d15` `o 34 test d16` `o 34 test d15` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(1) the application is made and served in time` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` `o 34 test d15` `o 34 test d15` `o 34 test d15` EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 4(2): in writing.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(2) the agreement or permission is in writing as paragraph (1) requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(2) the agreement or permission is in writing as paragraph (1) requires` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 4(3): where the application is made without the agreement in writing of all the others but with the tribunal's permission.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(3) the duty arises that the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(3) the duty arises that the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(3) the duty arises that the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(3) the duty arises that the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(3) the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(3) the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(3) the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 4(3) the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- application to set aside an award`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(1) the application to set aside an award must be supported by an affidavit stating the grounds` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(1) the application to set aside an award must be supported by an affidavit stating the grounds` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(1) the application to set aside an award is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(1) the application to set aside an award is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(1) the application to set aside an award is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 48` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(1) the application to set aside an award is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds` `o 34 r 2 test kind s 45` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(2)(a) the applicant is referred to in this Order as the claimant` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(2)(a) the applicant is referred to in this Order as the claimant` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 5(2): the supporting affidavit, each limb missing in turn.
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(2) the supporting affidavit meets the requirements` (`o 34 r 5(2) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(2) the supporting affidavit meets the requirements` (`o 34 r 5(2) test affidavit` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(2) the supporting affidavit meets the requirements` (`o 34 r 5(2) test affidavit` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(2) the supporting affidavit meets the requirements` (`o 34 r 5(2) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(2) the supporting affidavit meets the requirements` (`o 34 r 5(2) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 34 r 5(2) the supporting affidavit meets the requirements` (`o 34 r 5(2) test affidavit` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- r 5(3): within 14 days after being served, the defendant who wishes to oppose must file an affidavit.
#ASSERT (`o 34 r 5(3) the period for the defendant's affidavit`'s `period length`) EQUALS 14
