-- r 14(4), the SHANT: the award is not to be enforced until after the period.  Enforcing on day 14 is a breach.
-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `o 34 r 14(4) the bar on enforcing the award` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 34 r 14(4) the creditor` DOES `o 34 r 14(4) enforce the award` AT 14

-- expect: BREACH
#TRACE `o 34 r 14(4) the bar on enforcing the award` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 34 r 14(4) the creditor` DOES `o 34 r 14(4) enforce the award` AT 3

-- enforcing on day 15, after the period, breaches nothing.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 34 r 14(4) the bar on enforcing the award` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 34 r 14(4) the creditor` DOES `o 34 r 14(4) enforce the award` AT 15

-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 34 r 14(4) the bar on enforcing the award` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15

-- r 14(4), the MAY: the debtor's permission to apply.  On main a MAY with no LEST is FULFILLED whether or not the
-- debtor uses it, so both traces read FULFILLED; the closing of the window is carried by the decision function
-- `o 34 r 14(4) the debtor's application to set aside the order is made in time`, which answers JUST FALSE on day 15.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 34 r 14(4) the debtor's permission to apply to set aside the order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 34 r 14(4) the debtor` DOES `o 34 r 14(4) apply to set aside the order` AT 14

-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `o 34 r 14(4) the debtor's permission to apply to set aside the order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `o 34 r 14(4) the debtor` DOES `o 34 r 14(4) apply to set aside the order` AT 15
